# T-05 / A6 evidence — moon_ua_parser_mars example app (mw2)
# Date: 2026-09-13
# Worktree: F:\moonbit比赛\moon_ua_parser_wt_framework
# Branch: feat/v02-framework-middleware
# Toolchain: moon 0.1.20260904, --target native
#
# Command (one command, from the workspace root):
#
#     $ moon run moon_ua_parser_mars/examples/ua_echo --target native
#
# Exit code: 0 (bounded run: the example dispatches exactly four requests
# over an ephemeral 127.0.0.1 listener and closes it via `defer srv.close()`
# when the task-group body exits — nothing stays resident; the foreground
# command was additionally wrapped in a 90 s timeout)
#
# What this shows (R6): the middleware is registered on a real mars Server
# together with the framework's own logger_simple middleware (the `--> Get
# /probe` lines are mars's log channel; mizchi/mars logs the method in
# capitalized form "Get"); four requests are dispatched through the
# framework's own network stack (mizchi/x native HTTP server + raw-socket
# client, because the mizchi/x HTTP client would merge its own default
# User-Agent into the request).
# - Requests 1-3 (real UAs): the handler reads the three mounted groups
#   browser / os / device back from the typed Variables mount (ctx.vars)
#   via @moon_ua_parser_mars.mounted_ua_info; families match the uap-core
#   goldens cited in integration_test.mbt.
# - Request 4 (malformed, SYNTHETIC UA "SomethingWeNeverKnewExisted",
#   not from any uap-core golden file): the default console forensics (FO)
#   channel emits the {ua_summary, reason} record (line prefixed
#   [moon_ua_parser]) BEFORE the request block, the response status stays
#   200 (non-5xx), and the mounted families are empty (empty UaInfo) —
#   degradation per spec §3, semantics entirely from
#   vicoproplus/moon_ua_parser_middleware_core. The FO line shares the
#   println sink with mars's own logger middleware output.
#
